From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:23:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] perf(canvas): culled frames are shells, a pan is one
 transform, documents boot in turn

Profiled with Chrome traces on a 188-frame page of real screens
(frames out of process, as in desktop Chrome). Editor main thread,
v0.12.0 -> this: pan at fit 2260 -> 245 ms (37 slow frames -> 0), zoom
8% -> 60% 1700 -> 480-540 ms, pan at 60% 1780 -> 715 ms, fit jump
390 -> 125 ms; opening the page 10.4 -> 2.2 s of renderer CPU and
116 -> 27 MB of editor heap.

- FrameShell: a frame without a live document is its preview and its
  name (5 elements, no handlers, 2 subscriptions) instead of a FrameView
  (~40 hooks, a context menu, ~45 elements). A press on a shell wakes it
  from a window capture listener and is re-delivered to the FrameView, so
  select, drag and the context menu work in the same gesture.
- fix: a press on a frame showing its preview went down the layer path,
  waited for a document that is not there and was dropped; it is the
  frame's at once.
- The camera's offset (--vx/--vy) is set on the label layer, its only
  reader, not on the stage where it restyled every element per pan frame;
  zoom-only DOM writes are skipped while the zoom is unchanged; the stage's
  size comes from its ResizeObserver, not a layout read after style writes.
- FrameContextMenu reads its group facts only while its menu is open: they
  walked every frame, for every mounted frame, on every store update.
- Documents boot two per animation frame, nearest first; a large selection
  pins no documents; canvas elements never count against the live cap.
- Previews load lazily and retry on error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
